    {
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "type": "msg",
      "raw_time": false,
      "time": 1789665343.5791295,
      "body": "No \u2014 this file uses package-relative imports (`from downstream_apps.solar_event.configs import ...`), so running it directly as `python 3_finetune_template_1D.py` will fail with a `ModuleNotFoundError`/`ImportError` since it's not being run as part of the `downstream_apps` package.\n\nRun it as a module from the **repo root** (`surya_workshop/`), not from inside `downstream_apps/solar_event/`:\n\n```bash\ncd /home/jovyan/surya_workshop\nCUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python -m downstream_apps.solar_event.3_finetune_template_1D\n```\n\nNo arguments needed for a default run \u2014 `--config` defaults to this app's own `configs/config_script.yaml`. Useful optional flags: `--no-wandb` (skip WandB), `--max-epochs N`, `--batch-size N`, `--train_baseline` (simple linear baseline instead of HelioSpectformer).\n\nOne catch: as-is, it'll hit the bugs I found \u2014 the broken `metrics` dict (`SyntaxError`) and `load_flare_config` (`NameError`) \u2014 before it gets anywhere. Want me to apply those fixes now so you can actually run it?",
