      "type": "msg",
      "id": "7fc840b2-8b33-49f3-876f-db3f706127cd",
      "body": "Good progress on two of the three \u2014 `load_flare_config` \u2192 `solar_event_config`, and the `ds_flare_index_path` hack is gone \u2014 but the `metrics` dict is still broken and the file doesn't even parse:\n\n```\nSyntaxError: invalid syntax. Perhaps you forgot a comma?\n  train_loss_metrics : SolarEventMetrics(\"train_loss\")\n```\n\nYou changed `=` to `:`, but dict entries also need **commas between them**, and the keys need to be **string literals** (`\"train_loss\"`), not bare names like `train_loss_metrics` \u2014 those aren't defined anywhere, so even with commas added it would raise `NameError`. The keys are used later by `SolarEventLightningModule` to look up `\"train_loss\"`/`\"val_loss\"`/etc. by name (see how `build_trainer` monitors `\"val_loss\"` on line 202).\n\nFix it to:\n```python\nmetrics = {\n    \"train_loss\": SolarEventMetrics(\"train_loss\"),\n    # val_loss is the quantity logged as \"val_loss\" and used to pick the best checkpoint.\n    \"val_loss\": SolarEventMetrics(\"val_loss\"),\n    \"train_metrics\": SolarEventMetrics(\"train_metrics\"),\n    # Reported only: val_metrics do NOT influence checkpoint selection.\n    \"val_metrics\": SolarEventMetrics(\"val_metrics\"),\n}\n```\n\nAlso, I still haven't seen you fix bug #3 \u2014 `PATH_FIELDS` in `downstream_apps/solar_event/configs.py` still lists `\"flare_index_path\"` instead of `\"solar_event_path\"`. You removed the `f\"data/{...}\"` hack in the script (good), but without the `PATH_FIELDS` fix, `cfg.data.solar_event_path` is never resolved to an absolute path \u2014 it'll stay as the raw string `../data/solar_event_data2.csv` from the YAML, which won't resolve correctly when run from the repo root. Want me to check that file and apply both remaining fixes?",
