      "raw_time": false,
      "body": "That makes sense \u2014 it's not required to match the config field name. `build_helio_dataloaders()` just forwards `**task_kwargs` straight through to `dataset_cls(...)` (`workshop_infrastructure/datasets/builders.py:136-138`), so `ds_flare_index_path` only needs to match the parameter name in `solar_Dataset.__init__`, not `cfg.data.solar_event_path`. Keeping it as-is is fine \u2014 you'd only have needed to rename it if every call site (script + all three notebooks) got updated consistently, which is easy to miss and probably what broke it. No action needed there; I'll leave the docstring line 21 mismatch alone too since it's just cosmetic.\n\nThat closes out bug #3 \u2014 everything is consistent now.",
      "mentions": [],
      "type": "msg"
    },
