      "body": "Yes \u2014 the `surya_ws` conda env already exists (at `/home/jovyan/envs/surya_ws`) but your shell is currently using the `notebook` env instead, which doesn't have `lightning` installed. Activate the right one before running:\n\n```bash\nconda activate surya_ws\ncd /home/jovyan/surya_workshop\nCUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python -m downstream_apps.solar_event.3_finetune_template_1D\n```\n\nIf `conda activate surya_ws` doesn't find it by name (since it was created at a custom path), use the full path instead:\n\n```bash\nconda activate /home/jovyan/envs/surya_ws\n```",
