      "id": "e8f50081-c999-492b-9dc1-83eb9bae86be",
      "raw_time": false,
      "body": "The dict keys still need to be **string literals** (`\"train_loss\"`), not bare names. `train_loss : ...` tells Python \"look up a variable called `train_loss`\" \u2014 since none exists, it errors. It needs quotes to be a dict key: `\"train_loss\": ...`.\n\nThese exact strings matter too \u2014 `SolarEventLightningModule` and `ModelCheckpoint(monitor=\"val_loss\", ...)` look them up by name, so `train_evaluation`/`validation_evaluation` won't match what those expect either.\n\nLet me fix it directly:",
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona"
    },
    {
      "time": 1789667465.5943098,
      "id": "f1aa36c5-ab5c-4b30-90e8-e10b043fd0c3",
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "mentions": [],
