                "option_id": "reject"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "other",
            "tool_call_id": "toolu_bdrk_011otKkfNrDXWctiRjf34n9r",
            "raw_input": {
              "cell_type": "markdown",
              "content": "## Rebuild the model and load the trained weights\n\n`build_model()` reconstructs the exact architecture the checkpoint was trained with\n(backbone + LoRA adapters + head, wrapped in `SolarEventLightningModule`) from the same\nconfig \u2014 including loading the *pretrained* backbone, which the checkpoint's weights then\noverwrite. This only works if `cfg` here matches what the checkpoint was actually trained\nwith (LoRA/freeze/pooling settings in particular) \u2014 a mismatch shows up as a\n`state_dict` key or shape error below, not a silent wrong answer.\n\nUnlike `load_pretrained_weights()` (which loads a bare backbone state dict), a Lightning\ncheckpoint bundles optimizer/callback state alongside the tensors, so it's loaded with\n`weights_only=False` rather than the `weights_only=True` used for the raw backbone\ncheckpoint.",
              "cell_id": "6591ffa7-9ac1-40df-a770-e2ca0cfda705",
              "file_path": "surya_workshop/downstream_apps/solar_event/4_confusion_matrix.ipynb"
            },
            "status": "completed",
            "raw_output": "(mcp__Jupyter_MCP_Server__add_cell completed with no output)",
            "title": "mcp__Jupyter_MCP_Server__add_cell"
          },
          {
            "title": "mcp__Jupyter_MCP_Server__get_cell_id_from_index",
            "kind": "other",
            "raw_input": {
              "file_path": "surya_workshop/downstream_apps/solar_event/4_confusion_matrix.ipynb",
              "cell_index": 6.0
            },
            "status": "completed",
            "raw_output": "{\"result\":\"a1490ed9-2430-4cb9-8e25-5c74d1d6e27f\"}",
            "tool_call_id": "toolu_bdrk_01Prp2ypsAdhFCjeY2nQVGWG"
          },
          {
            "raw_output": "(mcp__Jupyter_MCP_Server__add_cell completed with no output)",
            "status": "completed",
            "title": "mcp__Jupyter_MCP_Server__add_cell",
            "raw_input": {
              "cell_type": "code",
              "content": "assert CKPT_PATH is not None, \"No checkpoint found \u2014 set CKPT_PATH manually.\"\n\nlit_model = build_model(cfg, scalers, train_baseline=TRAIN_BASELINE)\n\ncheckpoint = torch.load(CKPT_PATH, map_location=\"cpu\", weights_only=False)\nlit_model.load_state_dict(checkpoint[\"state_dict\"])\n\ndevice = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\nlit_model = lit_model.to(device).eval()\nprint(f\"Loaded {CKPT_PATH} onto {device}\")",
              "file_path": "surya_workshop/downstream_apps/solar_event/4_confusion_matrix.ipynb",
              "cell_id": "a1490ed9-2430-4cb9-8e25-5c74d1d6e27f"
            },
            "tool_call_id": "toolu_bdrk_019b6MU37Vtk9hocXqjVs8ua",
            "kind": "other"
          },
          {
            "kind": "other",
            "tool_call_id": "toolu_bdrk_013rqZmmXQmYp43UyH8JnnRy",
            "title": "mcp__Jupyter_MCP_Server__get_cell_id_from_index",
            "status": "completed",
            "raw_input": {
              "file_path": "surya_workshop/downstream_apps/solar_event/4_confusion_matrix.ipynb",
              "cell_index": 7.0
            },
            "raw_output": "{\"result\":\"8d0b3a7a-69be-45e4-89e4-0f96b8359319\"}"
          },
          {
            "raw_output": "(mcp__Jupyter_MCP_Server__add_cell completed with no output)",
            "title": "mcp__Jupyter_MCP_Server__add_cell",
            "raw_input": {
              "cell_type": "markdown",
              "file_path": "surya_workshop/downstream_apps/solar_event/4_confusion_matrix.ipynb",
              "content": "## Run inference over the validation set\n\nMirrors `SolarEventLightningModule.validation_step`: apply `preprocess_fn` (only set for\nthe linear baseline) before the model call, then `sigmoid` the logits to get a probability\nof class 1. `forward()` itself does not apply `preprocess_fn` \u2014 only the training/validation\nsteps do \u2014 so it has to be applied by hand here.",
              "cell_id": "8d0b3a7a-69be-45e4-89e4-0f96b8359319"
            },
            "tool_call_id": "toolu_bdrk_01J6h4XtGXbEktMnTgvtF6Xs",
            "status": "completed",
            "kind": "other"
          },
          {
            "tool_call_id": "toolu_bdrk_01XtjWv3NW2hvc1wqdHgpf6S",
            "raw_input": {
              "cell_index": 8.0,
              "file_path": "surya_workshop/downstream_apps/solar_event/4_confusion_matrix.ipynb"
            },
            "title": "mcp__Jupyter_MCP_Server__get_cell_id_from_index",
            "status": "completed",
            "kind": "other",
            "raw_output": "{\"result\":\"99f7f240-87d4-4fdb-b08f-ba6d9cd37020\"}"
          },
          {
            "raw_output": "(mcp__Jupyter_MCP_Server__add_cell completed with no output)",
            "title": "mcp__Jupyter_MCP_Server__add_cell",
            "kind": "other",
            "status": "completed",
            "raw_input": {
              "cell_id": "99f7f240-87d4-4fdb-b08f-ba6d9cd37020",
              "content": "all_probs = []\nall_targets = []\n\nwith torch.no_grad():\n    for batch in val_loader:\n        target = batch[\"forecast\"].reshape(-1).float()\n        batch = {k: (v.to(device) if torch.is_tensor(v) else v) for k, v in batch.items()}\n        if lit_model.preprocess_fn is not None:\n            batch = lit_model.preprocess_fn(batch)\n\n        logits = lit_model(batch)\n        probs = logits.reshape(-1).sigmoid().cpu()\n\n        all_probs.append(probs)\n        all_targets.append(target)\n\ny_prob = torch.cat(all_probs).numpy()\ny_true = torch.cat(all_targets).numpy().astype(int)\nprint(f\"Evaluated {len(y_true)} validation samples | positive rate: {y_true.mean():.3f}\")",
              "file_path": "surya_workshop/downstream_apps/solar_event/4_confusion_matrix.ipynb",
              "cell_type": "code"
            },
            "tool_call_id": "toolu_bdrk_01JMV4mPzQXDLeVz4D6c9oAh"
          },
          {
            "tool_call_id": "toolu_bdrk_01R344FqiPNRKidy68LZHPvX",
            "kind": "other",
            "title": "mcp__Jupyter_MCP_Server__get_cell_id_from_index",
            "raw_output": "{\"result\":\"65f4fc39-aa75-4541-a53f-b176c8ee8759\"}",
            "raw_input": {
              "cell_index": 9.0,
              "file_path": "surya_workshop/downstream_apps/solar_event/4_confusion_matrix.ipynb"
            },
            "status": "completed"
          },
          {
            "raw_output": "(mcp__Jupyter_MCP_Server__add_cell completed with no output)",
            "title": "mcp__Jupyter_MCP_Server__add_cell",
            "raw_input": {
              "cell_type": "markdown",
              "file_path": "surya_workshop/downstream_apps/solar_event/4_confusion_matrix.ipynb",
              "cell_id": "65f4fc39-aa75-4541-a53f-b176c8ee8759",
              "content": "## Confusion matrix and per-class metrics\n\n`THRESHOLD` is the sigmoid-probability cutoff for predicting class 1 \u2014 lower it (e.g. to\n0.3) to trade precision for recall on the positive class, independent of any change to\ntraining (e.g. `pos_weight` in the loss). Do this after looking at the matrix below, not\nbefore \u2014 the direction of any fix should follow from what the errors actually look like."
            },
            "status": "completed",
            "tool_call_id": "toolu_bdrk_01RDj2PSidq1TtpJ55GN5bdx",
            "kind": "other"
